## Clean starter vs implementation

The **clean kit** ships only `src/test/fixtures/**` (fixture chain skeleton).

It does **not** ship security/logging helper implementations, sensitive-field lists, default visual mask selectors, or guessed JSON keys or locators. **Allure metadata helper** ships in the starter; **readable failure diagnostics** are wired on the first UI/API implement batch (see `docs/failure-reporting.md` and `.cursor/skills/configure-readable-failures/SKILL.md`). Sanitized HTTP attachments and redaction datasets are created when plans require them.

During **implementation**, when the feature plan section **Sensitive Data & Visual Masking** (or API contract) defines fields:

1. Create helpers under `src/test/security/**`, `src/test/logging/**`, `src/test/reporting/**` only when the scenario needs them.
2. Populate `sensitive-fields.dataset.ts` (or equivalent) with **plan/contract-backed names only** — never invent keys or headers.
3. Set Page Object `visualMaskTargets` from **discovered UI locators** for those fields — never guess `[data-test*="token"]` or similar.
4. Use explicit `mask:` locators in specs for `@visual` filled states, or document empty-state-only with `visual-empty-state-no-mask` in the spec.

Do not reimplement redaction inline in specs once shared helpers exist for that project.

Do not log raw `request.headers()`, `response.json()`, or `process.env` values.

---

## Framework helpers (create when needed)

| Helper (project layer) | When to create | Source of field names / masks |
|--------|----------------|------------------------------|
| `redact.helper.ts` | logging or attachments need redaction | plan + contract; generic Bearer/JWT string patterns only where format is known |
| `sensitive-fields.dataset.ts` | redaction/sanitize needs named keys | feature plan + OpenAPI/Bruno — **no guessed lists** |
| `safe-logger.helper.ts` | intentional console diagnostics | wraps redact helper |
| `sanitize-http.helper.ts` | Allure HTTP attachments | uses dataset + redact helper |
| `allure-api-diagnostics.helper.ts` | sanitized request/response attach in specs | uses sanitize helper |
| `screenshot-masks.helper.ts` | `@visual` with filled/generated data | **only** Page Object `visualMaskTargets`; no default guessed selectors |

Reuse existing project helpers before creating new ones.

Do not create helpers speculatively in the clean starter baseline.

